    "Backup check": "pools.recoveryCheckTitle",
    "Restore and withdraw": "pools.recoveryRestoreWithdraw",
    "This imports pool recipes, checks reserves, and then attempts withdrawals for eligible pools without asking again. Withdrawals use one-time owner signatures. Stop other copies of this wallet from signing before proceeding.\n\nThe checks reject known counter regressions, missing recorded counts, unreadable reserves, and reserves recent enough to suggest another active wallet. They cannot prove the latest signing state or detect every signature made elsewhere.\n\nTo inspect a file without changing anything, use “Check a backup file”. To keep a pool running, cancel, restore the matching current complete MinimaCore wallet backup, and verify its signing state. Older reserves may need an available archive or fresh proofs.": "pools.recoveryRestoreWarning",
    "Restore cancelled.": "pools.recoveryRestoreCancelled",
    "Restoring pools…": "pools.recoveryRestoring",
    "Nothing restored": "pools.recoveryNothing",
    "That file isn't a readable PandaPools backup — pick the pandapools-backup.json you saved from Back up.": "pools.recoveryPickBackup",
    "Reserves verified": "pools.recoveryReserveVerified",
    "Recovery needs attention": "pools.recoveryNeedsAttention",
    "Nothing was withdrawn, because no pool's reserves could be verified. Saved recipes remain available below.": "pools.recoveryNoneWithdrawn",
    "Saved recipes remain available below. This was a reserve check only; nothing was withdrawn.": "pools.recoveryCheckOnly",
    "Withdrawing restored pools…": "pools.recoveryWithdrawing",
    "Connect the node to withdraw the restored pools.": "pools.recoveryConnectWithdraw",
    "Restore finished · withdrawals submitted": "pools.recoverySubmittedTitle",
    "Restore finished · some pools need attention": "pools.recoveryPartialTitle",
    "Submitted requests still need on-chain confirmation and collection from the owner payout address. Check Activity and balances before treating funds as received.\n\nRestored recipes keep automatic refresh paused until the current wallet signing state is confirmed. Older reserves may need archive recovery. The checks cannot prove that no unseen one-time signatures were used on another wallet copy.": "pools.recoveryWithdrawNote",
    "How pool recovery works": "pools.recoveryGuideTitle",
    "Keep both a current MinimaCore wallet backup and your PandaPools recipe file. The wallet backup preserves keys and signing state; the recipe records the pool contracts.\n\nRestore the matching wallet in MinimaCore, then restore the recipes here. Check live reserves before spending. A seed or recipe alone does not establish which one-time signatures were used. PandaPools will not automatically recreate missing owner keys. Do not run two restored copies of the same wallet and sign from both.\n\nCoin proofs in recipe backups expire. If live reserves are missing, Recover reserves checks the backup proofs, this node’s MegaMMR, and your configured archive connection. The receiving node validates proofs before import. An empty local lookup does not prove the funds were spent. Recovery needs an available archive or fresh proofs; a recipe alone cannot reconstruct chain proofs.\n\nRestored recipes pause owner signing, including automatic refresh, until you confirm current wallet signing state. Check both reserve amounts and signing status before withdrawing.": "pools.recoveryGuideBody",
    "Waiting for verified withdrawal confirmation and an empty payout address. Older entries without transaction evidence remain unresolved.": "pools.collectionPending",
    "Could not save withdrawal collection evidence. Nothing was posted.": "pools.collectionSaveFailed",
    "Could not read withdrawal transaction identity. Nothing was posted.": "pools.collectionReadFailed",
    "Withdrawal confirmed; tracked payout address is empty. Check your wallet balance.": "pools.collectionCheckedEmpty",
    "This node does not hold this pool's owner key, so the pool belongs to a different wallet. Restore the MinimaCore wallet backup that created this pool, including its signing state. Nothing was posted.": "pools.detailAbsent",
    "PandaPools could not read this node's keys, so it cannot check this key's signing state at all. Check MinimaCore is running and paired, then try again. Nothing was posted. This says nothing about the key itself — do not change anything about your wallet on the strength of this message.": "pools.detailUnreadable",
    "This owner key has used all of its one-time signatures and can never sign again. Nothing was posted.": "pools.detailExhausted",
    "Your last signing-state confirmation could not be saved on this device, so owner signing stays paused. Free some storage and confirm it again in Pool recovery.": "pools.detailUnsaved",
    "PandaPools has no record of how many of this owner key's one-time signatures have already been used — the recipe was imported, predates that record, or was rebuilt from what this node could see. Signing the wrong one could expose the key, so nothing was posted. Restore the matching MinimaCore wallet backup — the complete one, including signing state — and confirm it in Pool recovery. A seed phrase on its own is NOT enough: it rebuilds the key with its counter reset, which is exactly what causes this.": "pools.detailQuarantined",
    "That file is not readable JSON, so it is not a PandaPools backup.": "pools.detailNotJson",
    "That file is not a PandaPools backup, or it contains no pools.": "pools.detailNoPools",
    "Nothing was changed. This check saves nothing, imports nothing and signs nothing.": "pools.detailNoChange",
